    <li><strong>Database and C Programming form the two-pillar foundation</strong> of the syllabus. Within these, DBMS concepts, keys, relationships, MS Access objects, data types, operators, control structures, and loops are the most consistently tested sub-topics.</li>
    <li><strong>A gradual evolution in topic sophistication is detectable.</strong> Later years (2021–2025) introduce or increase emphasis on: normalization, file handling, recursion, pointers, structures, ACID properties, binary search, and ER diagrams — topics that were rare or absent in early papers (2015–2017).</li>
    <li><strong>The {max_y} paper contained the most questions ({max_qt})</strong>, while {min_y} had the fewest ({min_qt}). The 2020 examination year is missing from the dataset, representing a gap that prevents analysis of pandemic-era exam adjustments.</li>
