    <div class="insight-card">
        <h4>2. Database Theory is Non-Negotiable</h4>
        <p>Database concepts appear pervasively across all three question types. Students must be fluent in: DBMS fundamentals, keys (primary, foreign, composite, candidate), relationships (1:1, 1:M, M:M), MS Access objects, data models (hierarchical, network, relational), normalization, and DDL/DML/DCL distinctions. These topics consistently appear in Long Questions carrying high marks.</p>
